OL,3,GNEWSAAssisted dying is now law - what
OL,4,Ahappens next?
OL,5,
OL,6,FWith the law to legalise assisted dying
OL,7,Fgranted Royal Assent and announced on
OL,8,FTuesday, it would be reasonable for
OL,9,Fpeople to think a service is just
OL,10,Faround the corner.
OL,12,FThe reality is that the legislation's
OL,13,Fapproval marks the start of a lengthy
OL,14,Fprocess of consultations, secondary
OL,15,Flegislation and logistical planning
OL,16,Fbefore assisted dying can be introduced
OL,17,Fon the Isle of Man.
OL,19,FThe work is expected to take at least
OL,20,F18 months, in line with the timeline
OL,21,Ffor implementing the island's capacity
OL,22,Flegislation.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB IOM NewsC Reg TVF Clean Feed
